N={
"berthommier25_interspeech":("Explain why the second formant bends in an S shape while a speaker moves through vowel-consonant-vowel syllables.","The acoustic trajectory reflects several moving articulators and planning regimes; a purely acoustic curve does not say which physical movement caused it.","Fit a curve to the spectrogram and treat the curve as a direct articulatory law.","Generate the same VCV sequences with an articulatory model, separate vowel transitions from consonant influence, and compare the resulting trajectories and locus equations.","The study uses the Maeda articulatory model to reproduce Öhman's S-shaped F2 trajectories and reassesses conventional locus-equation interpretations.","The acoustic pattern is an effect of coordinated movement: a model can test whether the pattern follows from planning constraints rather than treating it as an unexplained spectral shape.","The paper reports synthetic trajectories resembling the observed sequences and structured effects of articulatory planning.","Model geometry, trajectory planning, corpus, and synthetic-to-observed comparison limit claims; matching a trajectory does not identify a unique human motor plan."),
"dinh25_interspeech":("A real-time echo canceller may process only 10-ms frames, but each frame still needs enough surrounding context to avoid audible boundary glitches.","Long context can improve continuity but usually adds delay; short-frame training exposes boundaries that long offline examples hide.","Use long frames, add post-processing, or train on isolated short chunks and accept discontinuities.","Keep long-context information in each training batch while producing short-frame outputs, so the model learns continuity without increasing application delay.","The paper proposes Extended Loss for acoustic echo cancellation with short audio frames and limited latency.","The loss supervises the local output using context that spans frame boundaries; training context and inference delay are separated rather than traded as the same quantity.","The paper reports reduced boundary discontinuities and improved short-frame AEC performance under the tested real-time conditions.","Echo paths, frame size, batch context, hardware, and evaluation signals bound the claim; continuity on the benchmark is not proof of every room or device."),
"ersoy25_interspeech":("Speech models may represent concepts differently from text models, and a joint model may combine or distort those structures rather than simply inheriting text knowledge.","Latent concepts are not directly labeled; comparing modalities requires a method that exposes structure without pretending an interpretation is a measured neuron-level fact.","Inspect nearest words or report downstream accuracy and call the result a theory of concept formation.","Use latent concept analysis to compare speech-only, text-only, and joint foundation models and ask which conceptual structures are shared or modality-specific.","The paper analyzes concept formation in speech and text-based foundation models using an unsupervised latent-concept method.","Concept formation is treated as a representation-comparison problem: the analysis proposes interpretable structure, while cross-modal differences reveal what the training signal makes easy or hard to encode.","The paper reports comparative latent conceptual structures across speech, text, and joint models.","Model choice, layer, analysis method, prompts, and human interpretation bound the claim; a latent cluster is not automatically a human concept."),
"fang25_interspeech":("Emotion recognition should generalize when people express the same emotion differently, across audio and other modalities and across related tasks.","Individual expression varies with speaker, gender, context, and modality; a parameter-efficient update can share too little or force unrelated tasks together.","Use one shared LoRA update or train a separate full model for every emotion task.","Combine shared LoRA experts, task-specific experts, a memory mechanism, and gender as an auxiliary task to separate common structure from expression-specific variation.","MMLoRA is a multitask memory parameter-efficient method for multimodal speech emotion recognition.","The adaptation has two roles: shared parameters carry reusable affective structure, while expert and memory paths preserve task/person-specific differences instead of overwriting them.","The paper reports improved multimodal SER generalization over the tested parameter-efficient baselines.","Datasets, gender labels, task mix, memory policy, modalities, and expression cultures bound the result; auxiliary gender is not a complete model of individual variation."),
"fang25d_interspeech":("An audio classifier may need to learn new classes one at a time with only a few examples, without forgetting classes it already knows.","The class vocabulary changes and few examples encourage overfitting; a representation that works for old classes may not expose the right view for new ones.","Fine-tune on each new class and accept forgetting, or keep fixed prototypes and ignore representation drift.","Fuse multiple views of the audio and perturb parameters during few-shot class-incremental learning to improve coverage and reduce overfitting.","The paper proposes multi-view fusion and parameter perturbation for few-shot class-incremental audio classification.","Adaptation is a balance between plasticity and retention: multiple views supply evidence while controlled perturbation tests whether a decision is stable rather than memorized.","The paper reports class-incremental classification results against the tested baselines.","Class order, shots, audio domains, perturbation settings, and memory protocol bound the result; benchmark retention does not establish lifelong robustness."),
"febrinanto25_interspeech":("A deepfake detector must learn new attack types while remembering older ones, even when its memory buffer can hold only a small sample of past audio.","Uniform rehearsal misses rare acoustic characteristics and can make the buffer biased toward easy or common examples.","Store random old clips or retrain from scratch whenever a new attack appears.","Generate auxiliary labels describing audio characteristics and use them to sample a more diverse rehearsal memory during continual learning.","RAIS uses auxiliary-informed sampling for rehearsal-based continual audio-deepfake detection.","The memory is selected for coverage of acoustic factors, not only class labels; retaining varied evidence helps the detector update without collapsing onto the newest attack.","The paper reports improved continual deepfake detection over rehearsal baselines on new attacks.","Attack families, auxiliary-label quality, buffer size, stream order, and detector threshold bound the result; no finite memory guarantees future attack coverage."),
"hasumi25_interspeech":("A cinematic separator should keep laughter and screams with the speech stem, because acted nonverbal voice is part of a scene rather than an ordinary sound effect.","Existing datasets often contain read speech, so a model can learn the wrong boundary and remove emotionally heightened vocal sounds as noise or effects.","Train on reading-style stems and assume the separator's speech category matches film dialogue.","Build a dataset whose speech stem includes nonverbal vocalizations and test whether that changes separation behavior on cinematic mixtures.","DnR-nonverbal is a cinematic audio source-separation dataset containing laughter, screams, and other nonverbal sounds in the speech stem.","The dataset changes the category definition presented to the model: the target is a vocal event in context, not a narrow phonetic transcript.","The paper reports that conventional separators mishandle nonverbal sounds and that the new dataset improves the tested synthetic separation task.","Synthetic mixtures, labels, scene distribution, separator, and nonverbal taxonomy bound the result; real-film generalization remains open."),
"havard25_interspeech":("Haitian Creole needs speech models trained on its own sounds and data, not only a large multilingual model that may underrepresent its structure.","Large multilingual pretraining can help but may encode data imbalance; training a monolingual model from scratch costs data and compute and must be compared fairly.","Fine-tune a multilingual checkpoint and assume scale always beats language-specific training.","Pretrain monolingual self-supervised models for Haitian Creole, compare them with multilingual and French-based models, and fine-tune all for ASR.","The paper develops self-supervised speech-processing models for Haitian Creole and compares monolingual, multilingual, and French-derived initialization.","Representation quality depends on language fit as well as parameter count; a smaller language-specific model can win when its pretraining signal matches the target speech.","The paper reports monolingual models that are competitive with or surpass larger multilingual alternatives on the tested ASR tasks.","Data volume, speakers, orthography, model size, pretraining compute, and evaluation domain limit generalization to the broader Creole speech community."),
}
